      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increased calf swelling, tightness, and heat are not normal after only four days and could be signs of a deep vein thrombosis (DVT), a serious medical condition. You should contact your surgeon or go to an emergency room immediately to be evaluated, as DVT requires urgent treatment to prevent complications like a pulmonary embolism. Do not attempt to massage the leg or wait for symptoms to improve on your own.",
